{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The proof is correct but duplicates forward/backward construction and uses many nested `exists`/`constructor` steps. Tuple construction and direct `ChoiceBisim.bisim` witnesses reduce syntax and elaboration work while preserving the same bisimulation argument.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro h\\n  refine ⟨@ChoiceBisim _ _ defs, ChoiceBisim.choice h, ?_⟩\\n  intro s1 s2 hr μ\\n  constructor\\n  · intro s1' htr\\n    cases hr with\\n    | choice hbisim =>\\n      obtain ⟨_, hr, hb⟩ := hbisim\\n      cases htr with\\n      | choiceL htr =>\\n        obtain ⟨s2', htr2, hr2⟩ := hb.follow_fst hr htr\\n        exact ⟨s2', Tr.choiceL htr2,\\n          ChoiceBisim.bisim (hb.le_bisimilarity _ _ hr2)⟩\\n      | choiceR htr =>\\n        exact ⟨s1', Tr.choiceR htr,\\n          ChoiceBisim.bisim HomBisimilarity.refl⟩\\n    | bisim hbisim =>\\n      obtain ⟨_, hr, hb⟩ := hbisim\\n      obtain ⟨s2', htr2, hr2⟩ := hb.follow_fst hr htr\\n      exact ⟨s2', htr2,\\n        ChoiceBisim.bisim (hb.le_bisimilarity _ _ hr2)⟩\\n  · intro s2' htr\\n    cases hr with\\n    | choice hbisim =>\\n      obtain ⟨_, hr, hb⟩ := hbisim\\n      cases htr with\\n      | choiceL htr =>\\n        obtain ⟨s1', htr1, hr1⟩ := hb.follow_snd hr htr\\n        exact ⟨s1', Tr.choiceL htr1,\\n          ChoiceBisim.bisim (hb.le_bisimilarity _ _ hr1)⟩\\n      | choiceR htr =>\\n        exact ⟨s2', Tr.choiceR htr,\\n          ChoiceBisim.bisim HomBisimilarity.refl⟩\\n    | bisim hbisim =>\\n      obtain ⟨_, hr, hb⟩ := hbisim\\n      obtain ⟨s1', htr1, hr1⟩ := hb.follow_snd hr htr\\n      exact ⟨s1', htr1,\\n        ChoiceBisim.bisim (hb.le_bisimilarity _ _ hr1)⟩\"}"}}
